---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import mapShot from "../images/dinosaurs/exploration-map.png";
import findShot from "../images/dinosaurs/occurrence-panel.png";
import treeShot from "../images/dinosaurs/taxonomy-browser.png";
import puzzleShot from "../images/dinosaurs/dinordle-puzzle.png";

const appUrl = "https://paleomap.nelson-j.ch/";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Dinosaurs · Nelson Jeanrenaud"
  description="A personal project: a map that shows where and when dinosaur fossils have actually been found, from about 250 million years ago to the end of the age of dinosaurs."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <span id="top"></span>

  <main class="wrap dino">
    <!-- ───────────────── Head ───────────────── -->
    <section class="section dino__head" aria-label="Dinosaurs">
      <p class="kicker">Side project</p>
      <h1 class="dino__title">A map of the dinosaurs</h1>
      <p class="lead dino__tagline">
        Where — and when — dinosaur fossils have actually been dug up, across
        the roughly 180 million years dinosaurs walked the Earth.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ───────────────── Screenshots ───────────────── -->
    <section class="section dino__carousel-section" aria-label="Screenshots of the app">
      <div class="dino__carousel">
        <div class="dino__track" id="dino-track" tabindex="0" aria-label="paleo-map screenshots, use the arrow keys to browse">
          <figure class="dino__slide">
            <Image
              src={mapShot}
              alt="The map screen: an old world map with colourful dots marking dinosaur fossil discoveries, and a timeline slider running along the top."
              width={960}
              loading="eager"
            />
            <figcaption class="dino__caption">
              Slide through time and the map redraws the continents to
              match — this view is set to roughly 72 million years ago, not
              long before the asteroid.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="dino__slide">
            <Image
              src={findShot}
              alt="A detail card open for a single fossil discovery, showing what it is, roughly when it lived, and where the information came from."
              width={960}
            />
            <figcaption class="dino__caption">
              Click any dot to see what it is, roughly when it lived, and
              where that information comes from.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="dino__slide">
            <Image
              src={treeShot}
              alt="A browsable dinosaur family tree, from broad groups down to individual species."
              width={960}
            />
            <figcaption class="dino__caption">
              A family tree you can browse — from big groups like "armoured
              dinosaurs" down to individual species.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="dino__slide">
            <Image
              src={puzzleShot}
              alt="A daily dinosaur-guessing puzzle called Dinordle, styled after the word game Wordle."
              width={960}
            />
            <figcaption class="dino__caption">
              There's also a daily guessing game, Dinordle — like Wordle,
              but each guess narrows down a dinosaur instead of a word.
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <div class="dino__controls">
          <button class="dino__nav dino__nav--prev" type="button" aria-label="Previous screenshot">‹ Prev</button>
          <div class="dino__dots" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose a screenshot">
            <button class="dino__dot" type="button" aria-current="true" aria-label="Screenshot 1 of 4"></button>
            <button class="dino__dot" type="button" aria-current="false" aria-label="Screenshot 2 of 4"></button>
            <button class="dino__dot" type="button" aria-current="false" aria-label="Screenshot 3 of 4"></button>
            <button class="dino__dot" type="button" aria-current="false" aria-label="Screenshot 4 of 4"></button>
          </div>
          <button class="dino__nav dino__nav--next" type="button" aria-label="Next screenshot">Next ›</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ───────────────── Story ───────────────── -->
    <section class="section dino__body">
      <p>
        A while back I got curious about dinosaurs again — properly curious,
        not just "big lizard, roar." I wanted to know where they actually
        lived, and that turned out to be a surprisingly tricky question,
        because the continents themselves were in completely different places
        back then. The land was still drifting apart while dinosaurs were
        around, so a present-day map is the wrong map to use.
      </p>
      <p>
        So, as a hobby project, I built one that isn't. It's a map that
        redraws the continents the way scientists believe they looked at any
        point from about 250 million years ago up to the asteroid impact that
        ended the dinosaurs' reign, with real fossil discoveries plotted on
        top. Drag a slider and two things move together: the shape of the
        land, and the dots marking where dinosaurs have actually been found.
      </p>
      <p>
        I tried to build it to be honest rather than flashy. A dot marks a
        place a fossil was dug up — not a guess at everywhere that animal
        might have roamed, which is a different thing and easy to blur
        together without meaning to. And when something isn't known for sure,
        the map says so instead of quietly papering over the gap.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ───────────────── CTA ───────────────── -->
    <section class="section dino__cta">
      <a class="dino__link" href={appUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        Explore the map ↗
      </a>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // A single-image-at-a-time carousel for the screenshots: prev/next
  // buttons and dots drive a native scroll-snap track, so it also just
  // works with touch swipes and trackpad scrolling.
  const track = document.getElementById("dino-track");
  const carousel = track?.closest(".dino__carousel");
  if (track && carousel) {
    const slides = Array.from(track.children);
    const dots = Array.from(carousel.querySelectorAll(".dino__dot"));
    const prevBtn = carousel.querySelector(".dino__nav--prev");
    const nextBtn = carousel.querySelector(".dino__nav--next");

    const closestIndex = () => {
      const trackLeft = track.getBoundingClientRect().left;
      let closest = 0;
      let smallestGap = Infinity;
      slides.forEach((slide, i) => {
        const gap = Math.abs(slide.getBoundingClientRect().left - trackLeft);
        if (gap < smallestGap) {
          smallestGap = gap;
          closest = i;
        }
      });
      return closest;
    };

    const goTo = (index) => {
      const clamped = Math.max(0, Math.min(slides.length - 1, index));
      slides[clamped].scrollIntoView({
        behavior: "smooth",
        block: "nearest",
        inline: "start",
      });
    };

    const sync = () => {
      const active = closestIndex();
      dots.forEach((dot, i) =>
        dot.setAttribute("aria-current", String(i === active))
      );
      if (prevBtn instanceof HTMLButtonElement) prevBtn.disabled = active === 0;
      if (nextBtn instanceof HTMLButtonElement)
        nextBtn.disabled = active === slides.length - 1;
    };

    prevBtn?.addEventListener("click", () => goTo(closestIndex() - 1));
    nextBtn?.addEventListener("click", () => goTo(closestIndex() + 1));
    dots.forEach((dot, i) => dot.addEventListener("click", () => goTo(i)));

    track.addEventListener("keydown", (e) => {
      if (e.key === "ArrowRight") {
        e.preventDefault();
        goTo(closestIndex() + 1);
      } else if (e.key === "ArrowLeft") {
        e.preventDefault();
        goTo(closestIndex() - 1);
      }
    });

    let scrollTimer;
    track.addEventListener(
      "scroll",
      () => {
        clearTimeout(scrollTimer);
        scrollTimer = window.setTimeout(sync, 100);
      },
      { passive: true }
    );
    window.addEventListener("resize", sync, { passive: true });

    sync();
  }
</script>
